  "notes": "そっち is a casual pronoun meaning \"that way\" or \"there\" - referring to a place near the listener.\n\nKO-SO-A-DO SERIES (〜っち forms):\n- ⟦こっち→こっち：02903_kocchi⟧: this way (near speaker)\n- そっち: that way (near listener)\n- ⟦あっち→あっち：02891_acchi⟧: over there (away from both)\n- ⟦どっち→どっち：02922_docchi⟧: which way (question)\n\nFORMALITY LEVELS:\n- そっち: casual/informal\n- ⟦そちら→そちら：00990_sochira⟧: polite/formal\n\nUSAGE:\n1. Direction/place: そっち⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{行|い}って→行く：00119_iku⟧ (Go that way)\n2. That one: そっち⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦しよう→する：00392_suru⟧ (Let's go with that one)\n3. Listener's side: そっち⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦どう→どう：00543_dou⟧？ (How are things on your end?)\nOften used in phone calls or messages: そっち⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{天気|てんき}→天気：00582_tenki⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧？ (How's the weather there?)",
